<name>SRS Airbag &amp; Seat Belt</name>
<section id="1000Y_S0012" variety="S0012">
<name>SRS Airbag</name>
<ttl id="1000Y_S0012_745Q2_T00B8" variety="T00B8">
<name>SRS Airbag System</name>
<para id="RM000002T13003X" category="C" type-id="8031H" name-id="554GT-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B1627</dtccode>
<dtcname>Side airbag sensor assembly LH communication stop</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000002T13003X_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00006A800000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The side collision sensor LH (for side airbag and curtain shield airbag deployment judgment) circuit consists of the airbag computer assembly, side airbag sensor assembly LH and airbag sensor rear LH. </ptxt>
<ptxt>The side airbag sensor assembly LH detects impacts and sends signals for airbag ignition judgment to the airbag computer assembly. </ptxt>
<ptxt>When a malfunction is detected in the side collision sensor LH (for side airbag and curtain shield airbag deployment judgment) circuit, DTC B1627 is stored in the airbag computer assembly. </ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Trouble Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B1627</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Short between terminals, open circuit, short to ground or short to +B in W/H between airbag computer assembly and side airbag sensor assembly LH</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag Computer Assembly Malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Floor wire (between airbag computer assembly and side airbag sensor assembly LH)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Airbag Computer Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002T13003X_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00006A900000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C159570J02" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002T13003X_03" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002T13003X_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000002T13003X_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00006AA00000">
<testtitle>Connector Inspection</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the battery negative terminal and wait for 90 seconds.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Make sure the ignition switch is OFF before disconnecting the cable from the negative (-) battery terminal.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Inspect the condition of the connectors connected to the airbag computer assembly, side airbag sensor assembly LH and airbag sensor rear LH.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>The connector is connected properly</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the connectors from the airbag computer assembly, side airbag sensor assembly LH and airbag sensor rear LH, and inspect the condition of the terminals of each connector.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>The terminals are not deformed or damaged</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0002" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0009" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T13003X_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___00006AB00000">
<testtitle>Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH Circuit Open Circuit Inspection (Between Airbag Computer Assembly and Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09843-18040</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST, connect terminals 4 (BBR+) and 3 (BBR-) of connector C.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146130J03" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>When connecting the terminals, do not forcibly insert the SST into the connector terminals.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of connector B.</ptxt>
<table>
<title>Resistance:</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.19in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.98in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2-8(BBL+) - 2-15(BBL-)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0003" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0009" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T13003X_04_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___00006AC00000">
<testtitle>Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH Circuit Short to Ground Inspection (Between Airbag Computer Assembly and Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Release the short between the terminals of connector C.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C101116J14" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between each terminal of connector B and body ground.</ptxt>
<table>
<title>Resistance:</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.19in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.98in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2-8 (BBL+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1M Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2-15 (BBL-) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1M Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0004" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0009" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T13003X_04_0004" proc-id="RM0550J___00006AD00000">
<testtitle>Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH Circuit Short Between Terminals Inspection (Between Airbag Computer Assembly and Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of connector B.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C101116J14" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<table>
<title>Resistance:</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.19in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.98in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2-8(BBL+) - 2-15(BBL-)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1M Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0005" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0009" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T13003X_04_0005" proc-id="RM0550J___00006AE00000">
<testtitle>Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH Circuit Short to +B Inspection (Between Airbag Computer Assembly and Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the cable to the negative (-) battery terminal and turn the ignition switch ON.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C101116J14" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between each terminal of connector B and body ground.</ptxt>
<table>
<title>Voltage:</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.19in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="0.98in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2-8 (BBL+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1V or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2-15 (BBL-) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1V or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0006" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0009" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T13003X_04_0006" proc-id="RM0550J___00006AF00000">
<scantool type="2"/>
<testtitle>Clear DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn IG OFF.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C161468J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the battery negative terminal and wait for 90 seconds.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the connectors to the airbag computer assembly and airbag sensor rear left.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Interchange the side airbag sensor assembly LH and side airbag sensor assembly RH, connect the connectors and install them securely.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When installing, do not subject the side airbag sensor assembly LH and side airbag sensor assembly RH to strong impacts such as dropping.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If a sensor has been subjected to a strong impact such as being dropped, replace it with a new one.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the battery negative terminal, turn IG ON and wait for 60 seconds.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), clear the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000050J01GX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0007" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T13003X_04_0007" proc-id="RM0550J___00006AG00000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Inspect Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), clear the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000050J01GX"/>)</ptxt>
<table>
<title>Result:</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.10in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC is not output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC B1623 is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC B1628 is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0012" fin="true">A</down>
<right ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0010" fin="true">B</right>
<right ref="RM000002T13003X_04_0011" fin="true">C</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T13003X_04_0009">
<testtitle>Replace Floor Wire</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T13003X_04_0010">
<testtitle>Replace Side Airbag Sensor Assembly LH<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000QG100DX"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T13003X_04_0011">
<testtitle>Replace Airbag Computer Assembly<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002RR0002X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002T13003X_04_0012">
<testtitle>Perform Simulation Method<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000ABY03DX"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
